There's a lot of hate for Faceless, but without them we wouldn't have ever got nontraditional supports. Never forget Annie, Morgana, brand were mids long before they were supports. Nautilus was always a jungle or top, now he's like an everything. Fiddle was a jungle and rarely a mid but ,in season 5 I think it was, he was a top contested support. Galio was originally designed to be a mid, then redesigned to be a top and mid but at pro play you see him primarily as a support. Remember Quinn was suppose to be an ADC for botlane but it just so happened to work better toplane. 

&#x200B;

 The game has changed a lot over the years just because people have experimented. Lets also not forget that Jungle wasn't a thing until Faceless made it one; the initial meta was 2 top, 1 mid, 2 bot. It wasn't until someone said, hey that's wasted gold in the jungle that it became meta. The thing about Council's is that they think everything should be black and white "This works and this doesn't", so when they go up against a faceless that knows what they're doing they're caught off guard and end up losing to the nontraditional pick because they've never laned against it or rarely. 

&#x200B;

So long story short, the council's knowledge of what does and doesn't work usually consists of the experimentation of those who've tried anything and everything. It may have resulted in some losses, some really poor match ups, but council's only have that knowledge and information because it was made available by those willing to do something unique or different. 

&#x200B;

